<title>FRANCE: ADP import traffic up 10 percent in December 1996.</title>
<headline>ADP import traffic up 10 percent in December 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>December 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 48,320 tonnes, an increase of 10.0 percent on the same month the previous year, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Global ADP import traffic in December 1996, by region, with</p>
<p>percentage change on December 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		 2,642 tonnes   up    3.5pct</p>
<p> European Union	 6,142 tonnes   up   35.4</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	  1,124 tonnes   up   37.2</p>
<p> North Africa	     917 tonnes   down 29.2</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa   5,298 tonnes   down  0.1</p>
<p> North America	 15,812 tonnes   up    3.5</p>
<p> French territories   1,225 tonnes   down  8.6</p>
<p> Latin America	  2,088 tonnes   up   14.5</p>
<p> Middle East	    2,420 tonnes   up   14.2</p>
<p> Far East		10,653 tonnes   up   20.2</p>
<p> Total		   48,320 tonnes   up   10.0</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
